      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The fluctuation relations give exact, broadly applicable links between microscopic reversibility and macroscopic irreversibility. They are foundational results in nonequilibrium statistical physics.",
        "attribution": "Evans and Cohen established an early fluctuation theorem; Jarzynski and Crooks developed influential relations connecting nonequilibrium work to equilibrium free energy. Credit among these central contributions is substantial and identifiable.",
        "maturity": "The results have been tested across a wide range of systems and are now standard tools in theory and experiment.",
        "uncertainties": [
