        "Antoine Georges",
        "Gabriel Kotliar",
        "Dieter Vollhardt"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory made strongly correlated electron systems tractable through a powerful, general framework that connects local quantum dynamics to lattice physics.",
        "attribution": "Georges, Kotliar, and Vollhardt were central to developing and establishing the framework and its applications. The contributions are collaborative but well documented.",
        "maturity": "The method has been extensively developed, benchmarked, and applied for decades, with continuing influence in condensed matter physics.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The boundary between the foundational formulation and later extensions could affect how the achievement is framed."
        ]
      }
    },
