        "Charles L. Kane",
        "Eugene J. Mele",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and topological insulators revealed robust electronic phases characterized by topology and boundary states, reshaping condensed matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele supplied key theoretical predictions; Molenkamp led an important experimental demonstration of the quantum spin Hall effect. The ballot's broader experimental history includes additional contributors.",
        "maturity": "The phases and their defining signatures have been extensively studied and experimentally confirmed.",
        "uncertainties": [
