        "Rudolf Grimm",
        "Christophe Salomon",
        "Wolfgang Ketterle"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Strongly interacting Fermi gases created a clean setting to investigate universal quantum many-body behavior and connections to superconductivity and nuclear matter.",
        "attribution": "Grimm, Salomon, and Ketterle led influential experimental work on ultracold Fermi gases and their strongly interacting regimes. The wider experimental effort was international.",
        "maturity": "The systems are highly controllable and have been characterized through extensive measurements, though the connection to real materials remains a nuanced one.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The proposed scope should distinguish this achievement from earlier recognition of Ketterle's work on Bose-Einstein condensation."
        ]
      }
    },
